# Security

- Hash passwords with Argon2. Use short-lived JWT access tokens and rotating refresh cookies.
- Never log passwords, refresh tokens, API keys, or authorization headers.
- All mutating routes write an audit log.
- Integration credentials are encrypted at rest and read only by the owning tenant's adapter.
- Validate and size-limit uploads. Never execute uploaded files.
- Enforce CORS, security headers, and CSRF strategy for cookie-based refresh.
- PII fields (email, phone) follow consent and purpose limitation. Honor suppression lists before outreach.
- SQL is parameterized via SQLAlchemy. No string-built queries with user input.
